  {
   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Diseases that are biologically similar",
   "text": "Papers report that GM1 gangliosidosis (infantile form) also comes from a missing lysosome enzyme, the same type of problem seen in Niemann-Pick A [E9c78c68, E995e5af]. According to HPO, both Niemann-Pick A and GM1 (infantile) can cause a cherry red spot in the eye [E7792b85, E86d0e19]. Papers report that Gaucher disease also comes from a missing lysosome enzyme, the same type of problem as Niemann-Pick A [E9c78c68, E309fa8a]. According to HPO, both Niemann-Pick A and Gaucher disease can cause an enlarged spleen [E303baea, Ecdbcb6c]. Papers report that Krabbe disease also comes from a missing lysosome enzyme, the same type of problem as Niemann-Pick A [E9c78c68, E60744b8]. According to HPO, both Niemann-Pick A and Krabbe disease can cause poor growth, also called failure to thrive [E6a02f2b, Ea714350]. Papers report that Fabry disease also comes from a missing lysosome enzyme, the same type of problem as Niemann-Pick A [E9c78c68, E4b5796e]. According to HPO, both Niemann-Pick A and Fabry disease can cause vomiting [E42f8a3c, E39530fd]. Papers report that late-onset Parkinson disease can also involve a missing lysosome enzyme, the same type of problem as Niemann-Pick A [E9c78c68, Ece278e5]. According to HPO, both Niemann-Pick A and late-onset Parkinson disease can cause rigidity (stiff muscles) [E1de711d, Ea566976].",
