  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Groups, studies and trials that exist",
   "text": "A paper reports that the International Niemann-Pick Disease Alliance (INPDA), a patient group based in the UK, is a global network supporting people affected by Niemann-Pick diseases [Ef2a2426]. A paper reports that the National Niemann-Pick Disease Foundation, Inc. (NNPDF), based in the US, is a patient advocacy and family support organization dedicated to people and families affected by Niemann-Pick disease [E0d1f519]. A paper reports that Niemann-Pick UK (NPUK) is dedicated to supporting individuals, families and friends affected by Niemann-Pick diseases [Ea90e420]. A paper reports that the National Organization for Rare Disorders also has information connected to Niemann-Pick A [Ee76e501]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Sanofi is running a recruiting real-world study of a medicine called Olipudase alfa in infants under two years old with this disease, with a study site in the United States [E80354ec, Eb112f38, Ed83c864, Ee7c3f8c]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Azafaros B.V. is running recruiting phase 3 studies of an oral medicine called Nizubaglustat (also known as AZ-3102) that include Niemann-Pick A along with some related diseases, with study sites in many countries [E1599abf, E11ab202, E420c0c4, E26d58fe]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, the Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (NICHD) ran a completed brain-imaging study using methods called fNIRS and DCS connected to this disease, with a site in the United States [E0f510fa, E853499f, Ebfb87ac]. A paper reports that the Cure GM1 Foundation, a patient group for the related disease GM1 gangliosidosis, runs a patient registry called the GM1 Matrix [E0405d11, Ea9bb267].",
